Since in 2014 Facebook decided to make the instant messaging function independent of its platform, making it an independent application,Facebook Messenger has been growing in all senses, both in terms of the number of users (with more than 1.300 million monthly users globally) and in its new functions, progressively adding different novelties and functions with which to satisfy the needs of needs of all users who make use of it.
More unknown features of Facebook Messenger
Multiplatform It has been one of the most controversial movements because there are those who claim that it is part of a Facebook strategy to complicate a possible spin-off of its three most popular platforms, butFacebook Messenger now allows you to send and receive messages from the application itself with users of Instagram and soon it will also add the possibility of doing it with those who use the instant messaging application WhatsApp.
Privacy in Facebook Messenger conversations can be greater thanks to the option toself-delete messages that disappear when you exit the application, in addition to the application itself notifying you when the interlocutor makes ascreenshot. In this way, it is possible to have a greater protection of privacy on the conversations and documents sent.
As with other messaging platforms, in the application it is possible to have an end-to-end encrypted conversation with another user, so that the messages are encrypted, even the files exchanged.
During the coronavirus health pandemic there was a great boom in chat rooms, with applications like Zoom, which offer many possibilities when it comes to communicating. These are also present on Facebook Messenger, with the so-called Facebook Messenger Rooms, being able to create a virtual room from which you can share the screen to play or watch a movie.
Only Android users have this possibility, and that is because Facebook Messenger can be chosen as the default application for themanagement of sending and receiving SMS text messages.
Surveys are very useful to be able to gather information from a group of people or to decide something in common. The option ofcreate polls appears in group chats and allows you to set different options.
Sometimes it is much more recommended and accuratesend the location where you are instead of giving the explanations to the other person. Therefore, from the iconLocation In the action menu of the application, a map is opened that indicates the location and allows it to be shared with the interlocutor, making it possible for them to locate you and that point is accessible during60 minutes.
Both from the application for mobile devices and from the desktop, just click on the camera icon within any chat to be able to carry out a video call and thus be able to communicate with another person.
If you are concerned about privacy concerns, the security options include a control that allows you to activate the notification to the contacts if the user is online and available, and you can also configure the selection of who can from this menu Access to view the profile or its availability.
As we have mentioned, one of the ways you can get the most out of Facebook Messenger is by using messages that self-destruct. To activate it there are two different methods which are the following:
In the first case, it is accessed from the icon in the upper left part of the application, where you have to select the option in the upper right partSecret that appears with a sliding lock. It is time to select the interlocutor of the secret conversation and, once the message has been written, an image or video can be selected to be sent, arriving at the moment of activating the timer that appears to the left of the text box.
Using this option, you first access the chat function, having selected the interlocutor with whom you want to exchange messages that will self-destruct. To do this, click on the avatar of the interlocutor and in the menu that appears selectGo to secret conversation.
