The openness of sunscreen fabric means the rate of small holes interlaced by warp and weft of shade fabric, using fibers of the same color and diameter to weave the same texture, the ability to block solar radiant heat and control glare with a smaller aperture ratio is stronger than that with a large aperture ratio.
Sunscreen fabric with 10% openness can obtain good natural light and transparency, but its performance against solar radiation and glare is worse. We generally recommend using fabrics with 10% openness in some sun exposure directions (such as the north), and also in some colored glass curtain walls, which have obtained the best natural lighting and transparency.
