Looking at the market trend of window decoration products in European and American markets from the perspective of child safety
The pursuit of a better life drives more and more families to pay more attention to window decoration design.
But the following points about the hidden dangers of the rope window decoration, you have to know!
In September 2012, a 14-month-old baby girl was strangled with suffocation by pulling rope window decorations. Before the accident, the parents had put away the rope and placed it at the highest point of the window decoration, but still did not stop the tragedy.
(CWCPR: Corded Window Covering Products Regulations)
In July 2018, a 20-month-old boy was strangled by a rope on the window decoration near the bed. According to reports, before the accident, the window decoration was in a high state and the rope has been placed at the highest point, but this has not stopped the tragedy.
It can be seen from this that simply complying with previous regulations and standards cannot avoid such incidents.
New regulations in the US
"The new safety regulations for window decoration divide the existing U.S. market into two categories: custom and inventory, and require that all inventory items, whether sold online or offline, be improved to cordless curtains, or at least to an inaccessible height. ."
All curtains produced after December 15, 2018 must meet the new standard.
This standard applies to all window accessories sold and produced in the United States.
If products that do not meet the requirements are sold, the US Consumer Product Safety Commission takes enforcement action and may accept legal proceedings.
Canada keeps pace with security
Recently, Health Canada has also approved new regulations on cable-drawing window decoration, which will be officially implemented on May 1, 2021.
Physical requirements (the rope window decoration must comply with the following regulations on the parts and the length of the rope):
· The inaccessible drawstring must remain inaccessible under all circumstances (regardless of angle, opening and closing, etc.
· At any angle and pulled by an external force within 35 Newtons (approximately equal to 3.5KG), the circumference of the loop formed by the drawstring must not exceed 44 cm.
Chemical requirements: The lead content of each external part of corded curtains must not exceed 90 mg/kg.
