The common lock cylinders on the market are: ABC three levels, of which the anti-theft level gradually increases from left to right, and the C-level door lock has the best anti-theft. Class A lock cylinder:
This type of lock cylinder has a simple internal structure, few card slots, low price and poor anti-theft properties. Therefore, it is recommended that after buying a new house, it is best to check whether the lock cylinder of your own door lock is Class A.
Different from the A-level lock cylinder, the B-level lock cylinder has better anti-theft properties. The lock cylinder contains two rows of slots, which can ensure that ordinary thieves cannot open it within 10 minutes.
The C-level lock cylinder is the best anti-theft property at present. Unless the door lock is violently damaged, the probability of the door lock being opened is very low.
