My source of inspiration for design is actually diverse, from sets and costumes in movies and plays, various element works at exhibitions, to some common objects in life, such as vases, trees, flowers and so on. I have always felt that design comes from life, and a good work must not be separated from life, and must closely related to life, so that users can like the work.
Now look back when you first entered this industry, is there any new change in your understanding of door handle design? Yes.
Recently, I have gained some new understandings. I try to combine factors such as the market environment, cultural heritage, actual needs of users and so on, to make some more forward-looking and artistic works.
At that time, I wanted to design some bold products with a sense of life and natural elements. However, due to my lack of confidence at the time, I didn’t start until this year.
And the CHEETAH, have you seen Animals World? Seeing the running posture of cheetah from the Animals World, I am very passionate and energetic, which inspires my creative inspiration.
The creative process from concept development, design drawings, proofing to the our R&D team to vote to decide whether to make a finished product, it usually takes 4-5 months. I usually start from the concept, look at other different elements, extract the core elements of a product, and then extend it by hand.
In our industry, imagination is very important, and imagination comes from these words: innovation, art, and wild brain. Maybe I am a very interesting person, and there are often many strange ideas emerged in the brain, and over time, my design also emerged in this style.
In the future, I want to be bolder and form designs with strong personal characteristics, so that when others see my design, they will say "Wow" for the first time. This "Wow" means amazing.
