Eufy continues to bet on the connected, intelligent and, above all, helpful home. In this case, we have to talk about those small, round robots that star in many videos on TikTok, usually because of the special dislike with which they are treated by other members of the household, such as cats.
For the rear The dirt tank remains, the water tank, which would be attached to the aforementioned one, and the mop that adheres with Velcro. We do, however, have an ON/OFF switch, something that has not been seen in this type of product lately and that is sincerely appreciated, especially if we plan not to use it for a long period of time, Eufy well pointed out.
We also have a gyro sensor for navigation, as well as a series of sensors focused on the robot not falling on surfaces at different heights. The same in terms of suction power, which will oscillate between 1.500 and 2.500 Pa according to our needs, the surface detected and the power that we have assigned through the application.
Once we have synchronized the robot with the application Eufy Home we will be able to alternate between four suction modes and a "scrubbing" mode. This device, despite not having a laser navigation system, uses a system called Smart Dynamic Navigation, that is, it uses parallel lines instead of a random system, which allows it to be more precise and efficient in cleaning.
The maximum noise it emits is 55dB something remarkable considering its suction capacity and the thickness of the device, and it is that one of the premises of Eufy is precisely to bet on a silent robot that goes unnoticed. Finally, we must bear in mind that we will be able to synchronize it with Alexa whenever we have managed to configure it with the application quickly.
With regards to autonomy, we are going to navigate between the 120 minutes that it offers us with the silent mode of minimum suction, following with 70 minutes of cleaning in the standard mode and approximately 35 minutes if we set it to the maximum suction mode.
At this point we are faced with a fairly versatile robot, which stands out mainly for being quite silent and compact, which far from other pretensions is limited to performing its tasks in a non-invasive way. The autonomy is sufficient and the suction power is remarkable, especially considering the dimensions of the device.
Once again we have to weigh whether it is worth buying devices at the same price that offer more features, or betting on a recognized firm whose functionality and durability are practically guaranteed. Meanwhile our cleaning, suction, autonomy and noise experience with this Eufy RoboVac Hybrid G20 has been good.
