Onomastics: the study of proper names
But even if we know what the real meaning of name day, he couldn't be left behind in showing us more. That 'more' will be an origin as well as a provenance of all the proper names that we use.
One of the most important branches is anthroponymy, it is also called anthropological onomastics. In it, what are studied are proper names and names of people.
As a curiosity, many years ago, the name that was given to a son were the first words that the father said when he saw him. While the Romans if they did not have a name chosen, they resorted to numbers.
Another of the disciplines, within the name day, which studies the proper names of places. Although not only these names speak of toponymy, but it is also common to find it in anatomy or biology.
